@startuml c2_agent_failure_routing
title C2 -- ALL failure sources now funnel through CallbackRouter

skinparam shadowing false
skinparam BackgroundColor white
skinparam sequenceArrowThickness 1.2

note as Sources #ddffdd
  **Failure sources -- all migrated post-C2**
  ----
  1. Community agent (HTTP, external)
       POST /jobs/{id}/agent-failure
       -> _get_callback_router().route(FAILURE)

  2. Backup monitor / Cloud Run Job (HTTP, internal)
       POST /internal/orphan/{id}
       -> _callback_router.route(FAILURE)

  3. Vast in-process monitor (thread)
       -> _on_failure closure
       -> callback_router.route(FAILURE)

  4. Modal in-process monitor (thread)
       -> _on_failure closure
       -> callback_router.route(FAILURE)

  5. CommunityMonitor (leader thread)
       Detects: group-terminal,
                machine-offline
       -> _on_failure closure
       -> callback_router.route(FAILURE)
end note

participant "any failure source\n(see list)" as Source
participant "CallbackRouter\n(callbacks/router.py)" as CR
participant "FailureHandler\n(callbacks/failure_handler.py)" as FH
participant "RenderOrchestrator" as RO
participant "RenderLifecycle\n.handle_chunk_failed" as LC

Source -> CR : route(job_id, FAILURE, error)
CR -> CR : is_job_terminal(job_id)?

alt job already terminal (idempotent skip)
    CR -[#888888]-> Source : log + return (no-op)
    note right of CR
      Filters double-fire:
      retried HTTP calls,
      multiple sources signalling
      the same job's failure,
      or a late signal after the
      job has already gone terminal
      via another source.
    end note
else job still active
    CR -> FH : handle(job_id, error)
    FH -> RO : on_job_failed(job_id, error)
    RO -> LC : handle_chunk_failed(job_id, error)
    LC -> LC : retry decision\nmark_failed\ndrain queue\nreconcile group
    LC --> RO : ok
    RO --> FH : ok
    FH --> CR : ok
    CR --> Source : ok
end

legend right
  Architectural rule (post-C2):
  No caller reaches RenderOrchestrator.on_job_failed
  directly. The only legitimate consumer of that method
  is FailureHandler.handle, which itself only gets called
  from inside CallbackRouter.route after the
  is_job_terminal short-circuit.
  ----
  This was the agent-failure migration's natural extension:
  if the rule is "every failure path goes through the guard,"
  then EVERY direct caller had to go too -- not just
  agent-failure. The orphan endpoint and CommunityMonitor
  followed in the same change.
end legend

@enduml
